WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.968 --> 00:00:02.434
-Welcome back to the show.

00:00:02.434 --> 00:00:03.901
And I want to thank you for
doing the Zoom interviews, too,

00:00:03.901 --> 00:00:05.868
as well, because
you're always there for us.

00:00:05.868 --> 00:00:08.100
-I loved it.
-I want to say, one week

00:00:08.100 --> 00:00:10.834
from today, Monday --
next Monday,

00:00:10.834 --> 00:00:13.667
you have the new season
of "Snowpiercer" premieres.

00:00:13.667 --> 00:00:14.767
Right?
-That's true.

00:00:14.767 --> 00:00:17.400
-That's a big day.
-True.

00:00:17.400 --> 00:00:19.634
-"Snowpiercer"
premieres next Monday.

00:00:19.634 --> 00:00:22.267
But it's also
your 40th birthday.

00:00:22.267 --> 00:00:24.934
Happy birthday to you, buddy!
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:24.934 --> 00:00:27.133
♪♪

00:00:27.133 --> 00:00:29.133
Happy birthday.
-Thank you.

00:00:29.133 --> 00:00:30.267
Thank you, thank you.

00:00:30.267 --> 00:00:31.734
-Do you have any plans
for your birthday?

00:00:31.734 --> 00:00:33.701
I know it's odd to make plans.
-Yeah, I don't know.

00:00:33.701 --> 00:00:38.133
I mean, we're in pre-production
for "Blindspotting," season two,

00:00:38.133 --> 00:00:39.801
which is a show that I write.
It's on Starz.

00:00:39.801 --> 00:00:43.100
Any "Blindspotting" people?
-Yeah, that was great.

00:00:43.100 --> 00:00:46.901
-Yeah, so we're actually
gonna be up scouting in the Bay,

00:00:46.901 --> 00:00:48.000
which is great for me.

00:00:48.000 --> 00:00:50.300
I get to be home
and see my family.

00:00:50.300 --> 00:00:51.934
Yeah, so that'll be nice.
I don't know.

00:00:51.934 --> 00:00:53.400
I'm trying to sneak my way
into a Warriors game,

00:00:53.400 --> 00:00:55.167
but we'll see how it goes.
-Yeah.

00:00:55.167 --> 00:00:57.267
Where are you from?
-I'm from Oakland, California.

00:00:57.267 --> 00:00:59.901
-Ah, Oakland.
-The show is set in Oakland,

00:00:59.901 --> 00:01:02.434
so we're scouting
locations up there.

00:01:02.434 --> 00:01:06.367
-I know --
This is for your 39th birthday.

00:01:06.367 --> 00:01:08.734
You had a cake and --
Your friends got --

00:01:08.734 --> 00:01:09.868
[ Both laugh ]

00:01:09.868 --> 00:01:13.334
I just don't remember --
What is this photo from?

00:01:13.334 --> 00:01:16.167
Because I don't remember
this photoshoot, but...

00:01:16.167 --> 00:01:17.767
[ Laughter ]

00:01:17.767 --> 00:01:20.601
Uh, I don't know what this is.
-Yes. Did some digging.

00:01:20.601 --> 00:01:23.033
That's -- That's --
[ Laughs ]

00:01:23.033 --> 00:01:26.701
I believe that is from
a short film that I did

00:01:26.701 --> 00:01:28.601
not long after college.

00:01:28.601 --> 00:01:31.534
I believe it is called --
-I believe -- it's so funny.

00:01:31.534 --> 00:01:33.300
-I believe it is called
"Rock Hard:

00:01:33.300 --> 00:01:35.601
The Rise and Fall
of Sexual Detergent."

00:01:35.601 --> 00:01:37.367
[ Laughter ]

00:01:37.367 --> 00:01:40.734
And I'm playing an I.T. guy
turned rock star.

00:01:40.734 --> 00:01:42.133
-Wow!
[ Laughter ]

00:01:42.133 --> 00:01:44.200
Yeah.
-Which is pretty much my life.

00:01:44.200 --> 00:01:46.300
[ Laughter ]
-And who knew about this?

00:01:46.300 --> 00:01:48.501
And who was --
-That is my friend --

00:01:48.501 --> 00:01:53.334
Yeah, Rafael Casal,
one of my big co-conspirators.

00:01:53.334 --> 00:01:57.434
-Yeah, exactly.
-Yeah. And our friend, Kim.

00:01:57.434 --> 00:02:00.767
Her sister has a bakery,
and they make incredible cakes.

00:02:00.767 --> 00:02:03.634
And that showed up at my house.

00:02:03.634 --> 00:02:05.000
-Well, give a quick shout-out.

00:02:05.000 --> 00:02:06.200
Do you know the name
of the cake shop?

00:02:06.200 --> 00:02:07.667
-Yes, Sweet Nothings.
Sweet Nothings Cake Shop.

00:02:07.667 --> 00:02:09.434
-Sweet Nothings Cake Shop.
Shout-out.

00:02:09.434 --> 00:02:11.567
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:02:11.567 --> 00:02:14.267
-Go get your cakes!
-Go get some cakes.

00:02:14.267 --> 00:02:16.601
They put your picture on a cake.
-Yeah.

00:02:16.601 --> 00:02:19.367
-You have good friends.
You bought a house

00:02:19.367 --> 00:02:21.601
a few years ago.
I think we talked about this.

00:02:21.601 --> 00:02:23.467
But recently,
"Architectural Digest"

00:02:23.467 --> 00:02:27.133
did a whole spread
and photoshoot of your home.

00:02:27.133 --> 00:02:28.601
Beautiful.
-Yeah.

00:02:28.601 --> 00:02:30.868
-But you said that you only take
credit for one thing only.

00:02:30.868 --> 00:02:35.367
-Yeah, yeah, the wallpaper
in our downstairs bathroom

00:02:35.367 --> 00:02:38.334
is my choice.

00:02:38.334 --> 00:02:40.234
Emmy Raver-Lampman made all
the rest of the choices.

00:02:40.234 --> 00:02:42.367
She's a genius.
I made this one.

00:02:42.367 --> 00:02:44.701
-Okay. Can we just --
This is a wide shot.

00:02:44.701 --> 00:02:47.234
This is a wide shot
of the wallpaper, but...

00:02:47.234 --> 00:02:50.634
-It's a very
Bay Area-specific wallpaper.

00:02:50.634 --> 00:02:54.834
It's all -- It's all, like,
particular Oakland

00:02:54.834 --> 00:02:56.634
or East Bay landmarks, really.

00:02:56.634 --> 00:02:59.901
So, you got, like,
E-40's on there,

00:02:59.901 --> 00:03:02.634
Mac Dre is on there,
Humpty is on there,

00:03:02.634 --> 00:03:05.734
The Bay Bridge is on there,
Joe Montana is on there.

00:03:05.734 --> 00:03:07.868
-Yeah.
-It also has local news anchor

00:03:07.868 --> 00:03:09.901
Dennis Richmond is on there.
[ Laughter ]

00:03:09.901 --> 00:03:11.634
Which is like a real --
You have to be pretty much

00:03:11.634 --> 00:03:15.267
my age and from the Bay
to know who KTVU News anchor

00:03:15.267 --> 00:03:16.968
Dennis Richmond is.
[ Laughter ]

00:03:16.968 --> 00:03:19.100
It's a real deep cut.
-This is Dennis Richmond.

00:03:19.100 --> 00:03:21.133
I don't know who --
I don't know.

00:03:21.133 --> 00:03:22.200
But he...
-Yeah.

00:03:22.200 --> 00:03:23.634
[ Laughter ]

00:03:23.634 --> 00:03:25.133
He's on my bathroom wall.

00:03:25.133 --> 00:03:28.167
-That is on your bathroom wall.
-Yeah, and we may be related.

00:03:28.167 --> 00:03:29.534
[ Laughter ]

00:03:29.534 --> 00:03:30.868
-Is that right?
Look at him.

00:03:30.868 --> 00:03:32.167
-He's a stud, yeah.
-You know?

00:03:32.167 --> 00:03:34.467
I'm trying to be like that.
-Why not?

00:03:34.467 --> 00:03:38.834
I want to ask how everything's
going with Clipping, too.

00:03:38.834 --> 00:03:40.234
-Good.
Yeah, we're good.

00:03:40.234 --> 00:03:42.767
We're recording new music,
which is exciting.

00:03:42.767 --> 00:03:44.267
-You are?
-It's super weird to, like,

00:03:44.267 --> 00:03:47.000
record remotely
during all the --

00:03:47.000 --> 00:03:48.901
you know, when everything
was scary and stuff.

00:03:48.901 --> 00:03:50.667
So, it's been nice.
We actually, like,

00:03:50.667 --> 00:03:54.501
got to get together in a studio
and start making some new stuff.

00:03:54.501 --> 00:03:55.968
So that's been --
that's been great.

00:03:55.968 --> 00:03:57.767
-Congrats on that.
And I've got to say,

00:03:57.767 --> 00:03:59.968
because everything you do --
you do so many things,

00:03:59.968 --> 00:04:02.133
but it's all quality.

00:04:02.133 --> 00:04:04.701
It's all well-done, buddy.
So congrats on that.

00:04:04.701 --> 00:04:07.601
-A man of your discerning taste.
-I do. Always is.

00:04:07.601 --> 00:04:11.300
So, yeah.
Best to the gang, Clipping.

00:04:11.300 --> 00:04:14.567
"Snowpiercer."
This next -- season three?

00:04:14.567 --> 00:04:15.667
-Yeah, season three
is coming out.

00:04:15.667 --> 00:04:16.834
We're shooting season four --

00:04:16.834 --> 00:04:18.501
like, we start shooting
season four soon.

00:04:18.501 --> 00:04:19.934
This is cra--
Do y'all watch it?

00:04:19.934 --> 00:04:22.000
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:04:22.000 --> 00:04:24.968
-"Snowpiercer" is good.
It is fantastic.

00:04:24.968 --> 00:04:26.934
-It's a little scary for me.
I can't, I can't.

00:04:26.934 --> 00:04:28.467
-[ Laughs ]

00:04:28.467 --> 00:04:31.067
-But, yeah, no,
it's been a wild ride, you know?

00:04:31.067 --> 00:04:32.367
That was my first --

00:04:32.367 --> 00:04:35.000
It was really, like,
my first TV contract I signed.

00:04:35.000 --> 00:04:36.467
I didn't know what I was doing.
I was like, "Yeah, TV?

00:04:36.467 --> 00:04:37.567
What's that?"

00:04:37.567 --> 00:04:38.934
And now we're like
three seasons later.

00:04:38.934 --> 00:04:40.834
-Really?
Because you did "Hamilton" --

00:04:40.834 --> 00:04:42.334
-Did "Hamilton,"
and pretty soon after that,

00:04:42.334 --> 00:04:44.968
like, I was -- like, I think
it was maybe the first thing

00:04:44.968 --> 00:04:46.434
I auditioned for
after "Hamilton."

00:04:46.434 --> 00:04:48.367
And then, like...
-I told you this before,

00:04:48.367 --> 00:04:50.467
but every episode, it's a movie.

00:04:50.467 --> 00:04:52.100
You're making, like,
tiny movies.

00:04:52.100 --> 00:04:55.300
I mean, actually giant movies.
But hour-long movies.

00:04:55.300 --> 00:04:57.801
-It is, like, really intense
and action-packed.

00:04:57.801 --> 00:04:59.868
-Yeah.
What's happening this season?

00:04:59.868 --> 00:05:02.467
-Oh, man. The --
I mean, if you remember

00:05:02.467 --> 00:05:06.334
last season, we --
You know, Wilford's back,

00:05:06.334 --> 00:05:08.133
and we separated the trains.

00:05:08.133 --> 00:05:10.234
And now, like,
I'm on a pirate train.

00:05:10.234 --> 00:05:12.834
And it's, like,
hot instead of cold.

00:05:12.834 --> 00:05:15.133
It's a whole thing.
Look, it's a big --

00:05:15.133 --> 00:05:17.267
-It's a big show.
-It's a big thing.

00:05:17.267 --> 00:05:19.334
A lot happens all the time.

00:05:19.334 --> 00:05:22.601
We're always throwing axes
and fighting death.

00:05:22.601 --> 00:05:24.467
-Yeah.
Jennifer Connelly.

00:05:24.467 --> 00:05:26.501
-Jennifer Connelly.
-She's fantastic.

00:05:26.501 --> 00:05:27.534
I want to show everyone a clip.

00:05:27.534 --> 00:05:29.434
Here's Daveed Diggs
in "Snowpiercer."

00:05:29.434 --> 00:05:30.834
Take a look.

00:05:30.834 --> 00:05:33.300
♪♪

00:05:33.300 --> 00:05:35.534
-I'm going out there.
-No, you're not. I'm going.

00:05:35.534 --> 00:05:37.567
-Neither of you
are going anywhere.

00:05:37.567 --> 00:05:40.067
-We can't stay here.
Ben.

00:05:40.067 --> 00:05:42.133
Ben, do you copy?
-We are not leaving him.

00:05:42.133 --> 00:05:45.133
-Layton, if we don't get rolling
right now, we will melt down.

00:05:45.133 --> 00:05:48.300
-How long do you need?
-8 minutes to get up to speed,

00:05:48.300 --> 00:05:50.534
10 to 12 minutes to run
a discharge sequence.

00:05:50.534 --> 00:05:51.734
-Great, go.
-Whoa, whoa!

00:05:51.734 --> 00:05:52.734
And leave you outside?

00:05:52.734 --> 00:05:54.033
-The breach suits
have 30 minutes.

00:05:54.033 --> 00:05:56.300
You go, you come back for me.
-We're staying here.

00:05:56.300 --> 00:05:57.934
-Yeah, like hell I am.

00:05:57.934 --> 00:05:59.434
♪♪

00:05:59.434 --> 00:06:00.601
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:06:00.601 --> 00:06:02.367
-Daveed Diggs.

00:06:02.367 --> 00:06:05.467
Season three of "Snowpiercer"
premieres next Monday,

00:06:05.467 --> 00:06:09.067
January 24th, 9:00 p.m., on TNT.

00:06:09.067 --> 00:06:10.634
And it's his birthday!

